# First Horde kodo from Harb Clawhoof (Bloodhoof Village).
# Sources: Forever client 1.60.1.70338 tables via wago.tools (ItemSparse: level,
# price, races, riding spell; SkillLineAbility: Riding); npcs.json and
# items.json for the trainer, the vendor and its stock.
# Forever riding: the client files every racial riding spell under one Riding
# skill (SkillLineAbility), so any riding trainer of your faction teaches it:
# Apprentice Riding (skill 75) from level 40, Journeyman Riding (150) at 60.
# Blizzard: learning to ride grants a mount, and training costs 100g at 40 and
# 1,000g at 60 (Kris Zierhut). ItemSparse lists the
# mounts at 20g (level 40) and 200g (level 60), usable by every race of the
# faction; whether a vendor still wants Exalted with another race's city (the
# Era rule) is server-side and unconfirmed.

step Learn to ride
  zone Mulgore
  tip Kar Stormsinger and Harb Clawhoof's kodos are in Bloodhoof Village, Mulgore. At 40 Kar Stormsinger teaches Riding (100g per Blizzard's designers), and learning it gives you a mount. The Forever client lets every Horde race ride these.
  level 40
  train 3690                          -- Kar Stormsinger, riding trainer
  skill Riding 75

step Pick a colour
  tip Harb Clawhoof sells the other colours (20g each in the Forever client). Buy any you want, or none if the mount you were given is the one you like.
  vendor 3685                         -- Harb Clawhoof
  buy 15277 npc 3685 optional         -- Gray Kodo, 20g
  buy 15290 npc 3685 optional         -- Brown Kodo, 20g
  note White Kodo and Lavender Kodo are new Forever kodos (level 40, 20g in the client) whose source is not known yet.
